# Actionpack writes `before_action` as `define_method "#{callback}_action"`
# inside `[:before, :after, :around].each`. Nothing that reads only the `def`
# keyword can see it, which is why `before_action` in a controller was 250 of
# discourse's declined app sites and — unusually — had **no candidate at all**.
#
# The second half is the guard. `NAMES.each` iterates a constant, whose value is
# a different blob's fact, so `after_hook` stays unknown. A name half-guessed is
# worse than a name not offered: the lookup would find it and stop.
def app.rb:20:3 status=resolved owner=Callbacks::ClassMethods site=app.rb:6
def app.rb:21:3 status=residue candidates=0
symbols app.rb Callbacks,ClassMethods,before_step,after_step,Widget
